# TradeFlow Project Cursor Rules
Single-owner local-first Import/Export operations and outreach platform.

## 🛠️ Stack & Styling Constraints
- **Stack**: Next.js 16 (App Router), React 19, TypeScript (strictly no `any`).
- **Styling**: Vanilla CSS in [src/app/globals.css](file:///src/app/globals.css) with CSS variables.
- **Forbidden**: Tailwind CSS, CSS Modules, CSS-in-JS, and React inline style properties (except dynamic numerical values).
- **Icons & Animation**: Inline SVGs only (no libraries). Apply `.stagger-item` for entry animations.

## 💾 Persistence & Portability
- **Storage**: Mediated EXCLUSIVELY via [src/lib/storage.ts](file:///src/lib/storage.ts) (local-first TODAY, backend-portable TOMORROW).
- **Restrictions**: Do NOT call `localStorage` or reference storage keys directly in components (use `STORAGE_KEYS` object).
- **Domain Mappings**: Group keys in `STORAGE_KEYS` mentally by domain owner with inline comment descriptors.
- **Serialization**: TypeScript types in `types.ts` must be JSON-serializable. Save dates as ISO 8601 strings, not JS `Date` objects.

## 📝 Conventions & Code Structure
- **React**: Next.js Server Components by default; `"use client"` only at interactive leaves.
- **Identifiers**: Every interactive element (inputs, buttons, modal triggers, links) must have a unique `id` attribute.
- **Paths**: Use absolute `@/*` aliases. No deep relative imports.
- **Commits**: Follow Conventional Commits format.

## 🚀 Verification Gate Pipeline
Run the following sequence in order before declaring task completion:
1. `npx tsc --noEmit`
2. `npm run lint` (If script absent, mark as: `SKIPPED — to be configured in a later prompt`)
3. `npm test` (If runner absent, skip)
4. `npm run build`

## 🎯 Scope Discipline & Pointers
- Only edit files listed in the "Allowed Files" allowlist. No unrelated drive-by edits.
- Never delete implementation_plan*.md / walkthrough*.md / task*.md. Move to docs/history/ instead. No rm in repo root.
- *Full specifications in [AGENTS.md](file:///AGENTS.md) / [CLAUDE.md](file:///CLAUDE.md). Test rules in [TESTING.md](file:///TESTING.md).*
